From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Collin Rose <collinr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] brcmfmac: fall back to legacy MBSS when interface_create
 is unsupported

BCM43602 firmware 7.35.177.56 does not implement the interface_create
iovar. brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if() tries versions 1 and 2, then
queries the supported version. When that query fails, the function
returns -EOPNOTSUPP and skips the bsscfg:ssid path immediately below,
which this firmware does support. A second AP BSS then fails, and
hostapd disables the whole radio, including the primary AP.

Set the version to 0 and fall through. The switch default marks the
iovar unsupported, and the existing bsscfg:ssid block runs. Firmware
that answers the version query is unchanged.

This change was first published for a Netgear R8000 on the same
firmware, as patches/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch in
88plug/netgear-r8000-plus (GPL-2.0). It is re-ported here onto
backports 7.2. The same early return is still in current mainline
Linux. It has not been sent to linux-wireless yet.

Upstream-Status: Not yet submitted to linux-wireless

https://github.com/88plug/netgear-r8000-plus/blob/netgear-r8000-plus/patches/861-brcmfmac-r8000-legacy-mbss-fallback.patch

Signed-off-by: Collin Rose <collinr@gmail.com>
---

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -758,8 +758,9 @@ static int brcmf_cfg80211_request_ap_if(struct brcmf_if *ifp)
 	err = brcmf_fil_bsscfg_int_query(ifp, "interface_create",
 					 &iface_create_ver);
 	if (err) {
 		brcmf_err("fail to get supported version, err=%d\n", err);
-		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		/* Fall through to the legacy bsscfg:ssid MBSS path. */
+		iface_create_ver = 0;
 	}
 
 	switch (iface_create_ver) {
